          "The 10.5% demographic gap (77.08% + 6.03% + 4.04% + 2.62% = 89.77%) almost certainly represents Alaska Native residents, making AK-HD-9 home to a meaningful Alaska Native constituency whose civic presence and economic participation are not fully reflected in the four standard Census categories. With a median age of 43.8 and the highest median income in the district data provided, AK-HD-9 is home to mature professionals — many of whom are Alaska Native entrepreneurs, healthcare workers, government employees, and business owners integrated into the district's economic and civic fabric. The narrow 54% margin in a district this wealthy and educated suggests that either the Alaska Native community's voting patterns differ significantly from the white homeowner majority, or that affluent white voters themselves are divided on governance priorities in ways that the Republican baseline does not capture. Either dynamic — or both — means that any candidate treating AK-HD-9 as a safe Republican seat is strategically blind to the actual competitive reality and the constituency composition that creates it."
