          { name: "Defaulting to Generic Democratic Positioning Without District-Specific Engagement", tag: "avoid", why: "HD-27's demographic profile—working-class, renter-heavy, with a significant Alaska Native population—requires district-specific legislative priorities, not generic state or national Democratic messaging. Alaska Native communities have distinct policy concerns (subsistence, tribal healthcare, state-tribal relations) that differ from statewide Democratic platforms; renters and working families have concrete cost-of-living priorities that require active legislative response. A campaign or legislative record that treats HD-27 as interchangeable with other Democratic districts will fail to build the authentic constituent relationships necessary to defend a 51% margin or expand beyond it." }
