          "Understand that 37% is not a mandate: the apparent multi-candidate Republican primary means Moore consolidated less than two-fifths of the district's Republican base. In a field where 63% voted for other candidates, any challenger who differentiates on competence, fiscal management, or responsiveness to educated homeowner concerns has a viable path to the primary. Treat the seat as perpetually at risk to a more polished primary challenger, not as settled.",
