          "The district's racial composition — 57.92% white, 13.72% Asian, 8.81% Hispanic/Latino, 2.73% Black, with approximately 16.8% unaccounted for in the reported categories (likely reflecting Alaska Native populations) — indicates an urban, cosmopolitan community where diversity is economically integrated rather than segregated. The 13.72% Asian population is particularly significant in a high-income professional district and likely reflects immigrant professionals, technology workers, and business owners whose presence in Anchorage's economy is substantial. The 2024 Democratic win despite Republican registration advantage suggests that Kaufman either consolidated the district's professional-class swing voters around issues of economic management, healthcare access, or education quality — the policy domains where affluent, educated voters with stable housing typically make decisive choices — or successfully mobilized the renter population and younger adults around different priorities. Understanding which coalition actually delivered the 48% is the critical strategic question for both parties in a district this competitive."
